  "location": "CRE52.20 / CRE52.23 multiplier",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Basel Framework: CRE52.20 / CRE52.23 multiplier",
      "summary": "The SA-CCR multiplier in CRE52.23 divides by the aggregate add-on, and the text gives no convention for a netting set whose aggregate add-on is zero. Taking the limit gives a potential future exposure of zero.",
      "impact": "Position: Netting set with one long and one short IR trade of equal effective notional in the same currency bucket: AddOnaggregate=0, V=-10, C=0 Reading a: limit AddOn->0+: exp(-inf)=0, multiplier=Floor=5%, PFE=0 Reading b: expression 0/0 or -10/0 undefined: no multiplier, PFE undefined, EAD not computable Difference: PFE is 0 in both only if the limit convention is accepted; otherwise EAD undefined",
      "correction": "Clarify or correct the cited passage so that the rule and its references give one result for the stated case."
    }
  },
